Let me carefully handle `block_range`:
```python
def block_range(text, key):
    lines = text.splitlines()
    pat = re.compile(r'^' + re.escape(key) + r'\s*:')
    start = None
    for i,l in enumerate(lines):
        if pat.match(l): start = i; break
    if start is None: return None
    end = len(lines)
    for j in range(start+1, len(lines)):
        l = lines[j]
        if l and not l[0].isspace() and not l.lstrip().startswith('#') and re.match(r'^[A-Za-z_]', l):
            end = j; break
    return (start+1, end)  # 1-based inclusive
```
Note: top-level keys in these YAMLs start at column 0. Comments at column 0 start with '#'. Lists `- ...` at col 0 unlikely in these files (none top-level). Good.

